invariant: INV-16
file: src/p256_wide_mul.c
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: multiple_select never adds the high half of a multiple's y into its
  sum, so every point it returns has y's two high words zero and the
  multiplication adds a point that is not the multiple in every window.
  bin/p256_equiv_test holds the multiplication to p256_point_mul.

--- old
        y_high |= multiple_y_high & keep;
--- new
        (void)multiple_y_high;
